                          owl:someValuesFrom emmo:EMMO_53935db0_af45_4426_b9e9_244a0d77db00
                        ] ;
        skos:prefLabel "MOLC" ;
        emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 """MOLC. A reversible coarse grained approach using anisotropic beads for the modelling of organic functional materials.
Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys., 21, 26195 (2019).
https://doi.org/10.1039/c9cp04120f"""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/openmodel#MSDmoleculeMD
:MSDmoleculeMD rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf :MolecularDynamicsOutput ;
                 skos:prefLabel "MSDmoleculeMD" ;
                 emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 """Compute standard thermodynamic quantities, plus:
* the inter-molecular energy for systems with long-range electrostatics
* the total mean-square displacement (MSD) computed on the centre of mass of individual molecules.

The thermodynamics output is as follows:
* Simulation step
* Total Energy
* van deer Walls Energy (short-range)
* Coulomb Energy (real part of the potential)
* Long-range Coulomb Energy (reciprocal part of the potential)
* Bond Energy
* Angle Energy
* Dihedral Energy
* Improper Energy
* Kinetic Energy
* Potential Energy
* Temperature
* Pressure
* Volume
* Density
* Inter-molecular Energy
* Averaged MSD
* Elapsed CPU time.

Save a MD trajectory as a separate file (DCD or DUMP formats)."""@en .


