###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/openmodel#SamplingInterval
:SamplingInterval rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf emmo:EMMO_d1d436e7_72fc_49cd_863b_7bfb4ba5276a ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty emmo:EMMO_faf79f53_749d_40b2_807c_d34244c192f4 ;
                                      owl:allValuesFrom xsd:int
                                    ] ;
                    skos:prefLabel "SamplingInterval" ;
                    emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 """In LAMMPS, the thermodynamic output is averaged and returned with *fixes* whose general syntax is:
fix ID group-ID ave/time Nevery Nrepeat Nfreq value1 value2 ... keyword args

The sample length corresponds to Nevery and is the number of timesteps used to sample input values."""@en ;
                    emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "Sample interval, used to sample the thermodynamic output."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/openmodel#SemiEmpiricalHamiltonian
:SemiEmpiricalHamiltonian rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            rdfs:subClassOf :HartreeFock ;
                            skos:prefLabel "SemiEmpiricalHamiltonian" ;
                            emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "Semi-empirical quantum chemistry methods are based on the Hartree–Fock formalism, but make many approximations and obtain some parameters from empirical data."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/openmodel#Slab
:Slab rdf:type owl:Class ;
        rdfs:subClassOf :PeriodicBoundaryConditions ;
        skos:prefLabel "Slab" ;
        emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A slab geometry in a molecular dynamics simulation is a type of boundary condition that is used to model systems that are infinite in two dimensions and finite in one dimension. For example, a slab geometry can be used to simulate a thin layer of fluid or solid confined between two parallel walls, or a membrane-channel system that spans across a water box."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/openmodel#Solvent
:Solvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
           rdfs:subClassOf emmo:EMMO_7509da43_56b1_4d7f_887a_65d1663df4ba ,
